4.1 Angular Momentum Operators
Now we have the eigenvalues of \(\hat{J}^{2}\) and \(\hat{J}_{z}\), we can write the matrix representation of the angular momentum operators in the eigenbasis of \(\hat{J}^{2}\) and \(\hat{J}_{z}\) as \[
\mel{j',m'}{\hat{J}^{2}}{j,m} = \hbar^{2} j(j+1) \delta_{jj'} \delta_{mm'}
\tag{12}\] \[
\mel{j',m'}{\hat{J}_{z}}{j,m} = \hbar m \delta_{jj'} \delta_{mm'}
\tag{13}\]
Now more important is the matrix representation of the ladder operators, which can be derived using the following relation \[
\hat{J}_{\pm}\ket{j,m} = c_{\pm}\ket{j,m \pm 1}
\] \[
\bra{j,m}\hat{J}_{\mp}\hat{J}_{\pm}\ket{j,m} = \abs{c_{\pm}}^2
\] Now lhs is \(\hat{J}_{\mp}\hat{J}_{\pm}=\hat{J}^2-\hat{J}_{z}^2\pm i\comm{\hat{J}_{x}}{\hat{J}_{y}}\),hence we have \(c_{\pm} = \hbar \sqrt{j(j+1)-m(m\pm 1)}\) so we have \[
\mel{j',m'}{\hat{J}_{\pm}}{j,m} = \hbar \sqrt{j(j+1)-m(m\pm 1)} \delta_{jj'} \delta_{m',m\pm 1}
\tag{14}\]
